    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0591" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg497"/>

                <head>No. 328.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 6, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 7.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letters<anchor n="†"
                        xml:id="d328-f1"/> of the 19th and 20th October, I have the honor to
                    transmit to you herewith reports from the Government of Canada relative to the
                    cases of the United States fishing vessels. <hi rendition="#italic">Pearl
                        Nelson</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Everett Steele</hi>, which I have
                    been instructed by the Earl of Iddesleigh to communicate to the United States
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>







